Vesper: a non-root caller sees a share's files as macOS virtio-fs reports them to it (TD-097).
virtio-fs on macOS reports the uid that asks as the owner of the sharing user's files, and the
System VM keeps those attributes for about a second whichever uid asks next. The server stats
each object as root before it switches to the caller, so a non-root caller saw every file owned
by 0:0 and could not chmod its own bind. A stat whose owner is not the effective uid is now
fetched again past the cache (statx AT_STATX_FORCE_SYNC), and each request stats its object
again once it acts as the caller.

--- a/attr.c
+++ b/attr.c
@@ -5,6 +5,10 @@
